From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:13:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AUTO_MEMORIES: read the views the lists name, not what
 memories/ holds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Before, every stage after synthesis globbed $(RESULTS_DIR)/memories for
*.lef and *.lib, the klayout tech took $(wildcard memories/*.lef), and
macro placement, regfile dissolve and synthesis read regfiles.txt,
inline.txt and regfile_cores.txt only if they existed. In a tree that
kept files from an earlier run, a .lib or .lef no longer generated was
read with the current ones, and a missing list was skipped.

Now each step reads the <m>.lib/<m>.lef of every module blackboxes.txt
lists, and the lists themselves without an existence check: a file no
list names is not read, and a missing list stops the step at the read.
The readers move from synth_preamble.tcl to util.tcl so OpenROAD and
yosys share them, and generate_klayout_tech.py takes --blackboxes.

On a clean tree the files read, and the results, are the same.

Carried in bazel-orfs for ORFS #4810, not upstreamed here; #4812
(0213) is written on it. Retires with the //:bump onto an ORFS that
has #4810.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
